\end{center}
Each row satisfies $s_n < \gamma \approx 0.5772157 < s'_n$, and the last column is exactly $\ln(1+1/n)$, confirming Theorem~\ref{thm:D} and the $\Theta(1/n)$ rate.

\section{Applications and significance}
\begin{itemize}
  \item A reusable diagnostic for constants defined as discrete-minus-continuous limits (Stieltjes constants, generalized Euler constants), separating convergence \emph{kind} from arithmetic \emph{readability}.
  \item The biconditional (Corollary~\ref{cor:bicond}) is the correct hypothesis for conditional irrationality-measure theorems.
  \item Theorems~A--C expose the shared logical skeleton of the proofs for $e$ and $\zeta(3)$.
\end{itemize}

\section{Discussion and future work}
\begin{description}
  \item[C1] No bounded-coefficient integer combination of $\{H_k, \ln(k+1)\}$ yields $0 < |q_n\gamma - p_n| \leq C\rho^n$ with $\rho<1$.
  \item[C2] Prove vacuity-free the dichotomy $\text{Irrational }x \Rightarrow (\text{Liouville } x \lor \text{finite irrationality measure})$ and instantiate at $\gamma$.
  \item[C3] Linear-forms transfer: small forms in $\{1,\gamma,\zeta(2)\}$ (resp. $\{1,\gamma,\ln2\}$) exist iff small forms in $\{1,\gamma\}$ do; study a two-variable engine $qx+ry-p$.
  \item[C4] A rational-coefficient accelerant $\gamma = \sum r_n$ with $|\gamma - \sum_{k\leq n} r_k| = o(1/D_n)$ would feed the engine.
  \item[C5] Width-optimality of the choice $f=n+1,\ g=n$ among brackets $[H_n - \ln f(n), H_n - \ln g(n)]$.
\end{description}

\subsection{The role of the Stieltjes constants}
The Stieltjes constants $\gamma_k$ are the Laurent coefficients of $\zeta$ at $s=1$:
\[
\zeta(s) = \frac{1}{s-1} + \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^k}{k!}\,\gamma_k\,(s-1)^k, \qquad \gamma_0 = \gamma.
\]
They admit representations $\gamma_k = \lim_{n}\bigl(\sum_{m=1}^n (\ln m)^k/m - (\ln n)^{k+1}/(k+1)\bigr)$ generalizing the harmonic definition and sharing its defect: discrete sums minus a continuous term with transcendental tails. The diagnostic of Section~6 applies verbatim to each $\gamma_k$, and conjecture C4 is naturally posed for the whole family.

\subsection{Why effectivity matters}
The bounds of Section~5 are effective: Theorem~\ref{thm:D} is an exact identity, and Theorems~\ref{thm:E}--\ref{thm:G} give computable envelopes, so the enclosure algorithm is a genuine procedure returning a rational interval around $\gamma$. Effectivity makes the obstruction analysis rigorous rather than heuristic.

\section{Conclusion}
We gave a rigorous account of the irrationality engine in biconditional, directional, and sequence forms, and applied it diagnostically to $\gamma$. The harmonic approximants trap $\gamma$ with exact width $\ln(1+1/n)$ and effective error $|s_n - \gamma| < \ln(1+1/n)$, yet---by transcendental endpoints and sub-geometric speed---cannot drive the engine. This is a precise map of a three-century-old wall, and a specification of the door a future proof must open.

